A:  MONEY     |  HISTORY   |  MONEY     
T:------------
T:A Detailed
T:History
T:------------
T:1. BARTER
T:Long ago,
T:people used
T:barter.
T:Trade apples
T:for shoes.
T:Problem:
T:Double
T:coincidence
T:of wants.
T:Hard to find
T:good trade
T:partners!
T:------------
T:2. COMMODITY
T:People used
T:valuable
T:items:
T:Cowrie shell
T:Salt, grain
T:Cattle, gems
T:Salt was so
T:valuable,
T:Roman troops
T:got paid
T:in salt!
T:Origin of
T:word SALARY.
T:------------
T:3. COINS
T:Around 600BC
T:Lydia made
T:first coins.
T:Made of
T:Electrum:
T:Gold+Silver.
T:Stamped with
T:king emblem
T:for weight
T:and purity.
T:------------
T:4. PAPER
T:Coins were
T:heavy to
T:carry.
T:7th Century
T:China made
T:paper notes.
T:Song Dynasty
T:issued
T:Jiaozi, 1st
T:paper cash.
T:Marco Polo
T:brought idea
T:to Europe.
T:------------
T:5. GOLD STD
T:Gold stored
T:in vaults.
T:Paper notes
T:were traded
T:as receipts.
T:Led to Gold
T:Standard:
T:Paper backed
T:by real gold
T:in reserve.
T:------------
T:6. FIAT
T:In 1971, US
T:ended gold
T:standard.
T:Nixon Shock!
T:Fiat money
T:has value
T:by decree.
T:Government
T:says it has
T:value, so
T:we trust it.
T:------------
T:7. DIGITAL
T:1950s saw
T:first credit
T:cards born.
T:1990s gave
T:online bank.
T:Today, most
T:money is 1s
T:and 0s on
T:servers.
T:------------
T:8. CRYPTO
T:In 2009,
T:Satoshi
T:Nakamoto
T:launched
T:Bitcoin.
T:No central
T:bank needed.
T:Digital cash
T:running on
T:blockchain.
